<title>USA: IBM reports better-than-expected profit.</title>
<headline>IBM reports better-than-expected profit.</headline>
<dateline>ARMONK, N.Y. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp. reported a better-than-expected first-quarter profit of $1.19 billion and cited a strong increase in North American revenues.</p>
<p>Net income, equal to $2.37 a share, compared with first-quarter earnings of $1.20 billion, or $2.21 a share a year earlier, when IBM had more shares outstanding.</p>
</text>
